window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-053.json",{"day":53,"title":"A Cooperative Shop and the Meaning of Trust","targetWords":[{"word":"monopoly","gloss":"垄断","context":"A village cooperative began as a response to a local monopoly in basic supplies.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"quota","gloss":"配额","context":"Members agreed on a quota for initial contributions and planned to keep any surplus for repairs before paying a dividend.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"surplus","gloss":"盈余","context":"Members agreed on a quota for initial contributions and planned to keep any surplus for repairs before paying a dividend.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"allowance","gloss":"津贴","context":"A small transport allowance helped volunteers reach an old mill converted into a shop.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"mill","gloss":"磨坊","context":"A small transport allowance helped volunteers reach an old mill converted into a shop.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"toll","gloss":"通行费","context":"Drivers still paid a toll on the main road, and workers expected a modest bonus if sales improved.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"bonus","gloss":"奖金","context":"Drivers still paid a toll on the main road, and workers expected a modest bonus if sales improved.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"affluent","gloss":"富裕的","context":"The village was not affluent, so an increase in turnover would matter.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"turnover","gloss":"营业额","context":"The village was not affluent, so an increase in turnover would matter.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"coupon","gloss":"优惠券","context":"Yet a colorful coupon could not persuade residents to ignore the risk of default on a loan.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"default","gloss":"违约","context":"Yet a colorful coupon could not persuade residents to ignore the risk of default on a loan.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"fiscal","gloss":"财政的","context":"Trust required fiscal discipline, not merely confidence in friendly neighbors.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"bankrupt","gloss":"破产的","context":"After a regional slump, several suppliers were bankrupt, and deliveries became unreliable.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"slump","gloss":"低迷","context":"After a regional slump, several suppliers were bankrupt, and deliveries became unreliable.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"installment","gloss":"分期付款","context":"The cooperative negotiated an installment arrangement for equipment and shared cargo space with a neighboring town.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"cargo","gloss":"货物","context":"The cooperative negotiated an installment arrangement for equipment and shared cargo space with a neighboring town.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"lottery","gloss":"抽奖","context":"A lottery might raise some money, but it could not sustain the supply of essential merchandise.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"merchandise","gloss":"商品","context":"A lottery might raise some money, but it could not sustain the supply of essential merchandise.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"auction","gloss":"拍卖","context":"Nor should an auction of donated objects replace routine planning.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"dividend","gloss":"分红","context":"Members agreed on a quota for initial contributions and planned to keep any surplus for repairs before paying a dividend.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"freight","gloss":"货运","context":"Members compared freight costs before deciding whether to levy a small charge for home delivery.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"levy","gloss":"征收","context":"Members compared freight costs before deciding whether to levy a small charge for home delivery.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"penny","gloss":"便士","context":"A penny saved on each journey added up, yet the lease still had to be paid.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"lease","gloss":"租约","context":"A penny saved on each journey added up, yet the lease still had to be paid.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"lucrative","gloss":"有利可图的","context":"The shop needed a financially sound model even if no part of its operation was especially lucrative.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"refund","gloss":"退款","context":"Customers received a refund when a product failed, and an independent audit checked that the policy was applied fairly.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"audit","gloss":"审计","context":"Customers received a refund when a product failed, and an independent audit checked that the policy was applied fairly.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"inventory","gloss":"库存","context":"Accurate inventory records prevented the purchase of goods already sitting in storage.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"trademark","gloss":"商标","context":"The cooperative used its own trademark but did not pretend that a label guaranteed excellence.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"portfolio","gloss":"投资组合","context":"It kept a limited portfolio of suppliers to balance flexibility with manageable administration.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"thrift","gloss":"节俭","context":"Thrift meant avoiding waste, not always choosing the lowest price.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"tariff","gloss":"关税","context":"A tariff could make imported equipment more expensive, while a useful warranty might justify paying more initially.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"warranty","gloss":"保修","context":"A tariff could make imported equipment more expensive, while a useful warranty might justify paying more initially.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"economics","gloss":"经济学","context":"Volunteers studying basic economics learned that the cheapest goods were not necessarily the least costly over their entire working life.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"goods","gloss":"商品","context":"Accurate inventory records prevented the purchase of goods already sitting in storage.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"accord","gloss":"一致","context":"Financial rules alone did not ensure that members would remain in accord.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"kind","gloss":"友善的","context":"A kind assistant might attract interest, but everyone deserved the same attention whether or not they knew the committee.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"interest","gloss":"兴趣","context":"A kind assistant might attract interest, but everyone deserved the same attention whether or not they knew the committee.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"attention","gloss":"关注","context":"A kind assistant might attract interest, but everyone deserved the same attention whether or not they knew the committee.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"love","gloss":"热爱","context":"Love for the village could support participation, yet a defensive attitude toward criticism would weaken it.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"attitude","gloss":"态度","context":"Love for the village could support participation, yet a defensive attitude toward criticism would weaken it.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"memory","gloss":"记忆","context":"An older resident's memory of a previous failed scheme shaped her opinion of this one.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"opinion","gloss":"意见","context":"An older resident's memory of a previous failed scheme shaped her opinion of this one.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"popular","gloss":"受欢迎的","context":"The cooperative became popular only after responding to such concerns.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"please","gloss":"取悦","context":"It should not try to please every person with promises it could not keep.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"hope","gloss":"希望","context":"Instead, its members could hope that clear information would gradually become a habit in their public decisions.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"habit","gloss":"习惯","context":"Instead, its members could hope that clear information would gradually become a habit in their public decisions.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"message","gloss":"信息","context":"The strongest message the shop sent was not that cooperation removed all uncertainty.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"fear","gloss":"害怕","context":"Residents might still fear rising costs, and a serious shortage required difficult choices.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"serious","gloss":"认真的","context":"Residents might still fear rising costs, and a serious shortage required difficult choices.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"A village cooperative began as a response to a local monopoly in basic supplies. Members agreed on a quota for initial contributions and planned to keep any surplus for repairs before paying a dividend. A small transport allowance helped volunteers reach an old mill converted into a shop. Drivers still paid a toll on the main road, and workers expected a modest bonus if sales improved. The village was not affluent, so an increase in turnover would matter. Yet a colorful coupon could not persuade residents to ignore the risk of default on a loan. Trust required fiscal discipline, not merely confidence in friendly neighbors.","zh":"村庄合作社最初为应对基本物资的本地垄断而成立。成员约定初始出资配额，计划先将盈余留作维修，再支付分红。一点交通津贴帮助志愿者前往改作商店的旧磨坊。司机在主路仍需支付通行费，工人则希望销售改善后获得适度奖金。村庄并不富裕，因此营业额增加很重要。然而彩色优惠券不能让居民忽视贷款违约风险。信任需要财务纪律，不只是对友好邻居有信心。"},{"en":"After a regional slump, several suppliers were bankrupt, and deliveries became unreliable. The cooperative negotiated an installment arrangement for equipment and shared cargo space with a neighboring town. A lottery might raise some money, but it could not sustain the supply of essential merchandise. Nor should an auction of donated objects replace routine planning. Members compared freight costs before deciding whether to levy a small charge for home delivery. A penny saved on each journey added up, yet the lease still had to be paid. The shop needed a financially sound model even if no part of its operation was especially lucrative.","zh":"地区低迷后，几家供应商破产，配送变得不可靠。合作社为设备协商分期付款，并与邻镇共享货运空间。抽奖也许能筹些钱，却无法维持必需商品供应。捐赠品拍卖也不应代替日常规划。成员比较货运费用，再决定是否对送货征少量费用。每次节省一便士积少成多，但租约费用仍需支付。即使没有哪个业务特别赚钱，商店也需要财务上稳健的模式。"},{"en":"Customers received a refund when a product failed, and an independent audit checked that the policy was applied fairly. Accurate inventory records prevented the purchase of goods already sitting in storage. The cooperative used its own trademark but did not pretend that a label guaranteed excellence. It kept a limited portfolio of suppliers to balance flexibility with manageable administration. Thrift meant avoiding waste, not always choosing the lowest price. A tariff could make imported equipment more expensive, while a useful warranty might justify paying more initially. Volunteers studying basic economics learned that the cheapest goods were not necessarily the least costly over their entire working life.","zh":"产品出问题时，顾客会退款，独立审计检查这一政策是否公平执行。准确库存记录避免购买库里已经有的商品。合作社使用自己的商标，却不假装标签保证卓越。它维持有限的供应商组合，平衡灵活性与可管理性。节俭意味着避免浪费，而不是永远选最低价。关税可能使进口设备更贵，有用保修则可能值得初期多付一些。学习基本经济学的志愿者发现，最便宜的商品在整个使用期未必成本最低。"},{"en":"Financial rules alone did not ensure that members would remain in accord. A kind assistant might attract interest, but everyone deserved the same attention whether or not they knew the committee. Love for the village could support participation, yet a defensive attitude toward criticism would weaken it. An older resident's memory of a previous failed scheme shaped her opinion of this one. The cooperative became popular only after responding to such concerns. It should not try to please every person with promises it could not keep. Instead, its members could hope that clear information would gradually become a habit in their public decisions.","zh":"只有财务规则不能保证成员始终意见一致。友善店员可能引起兴趣，但不论是否认识委员会成员，每个人都应得到同样关注。对村庄的热爱能支持参与，但防御性对待批评会削弱它。一位老居民对早先失败项目的记忆，塑造了她对本项目的看法。合作社回应这些担忧后才受到欢迎。它不应以无法兑现的承诺取悦所有人。相反，成员可以希望清楚传递信息逐渐成为公共决策中的习惯。"},{"en":"The strongest message the shop sent was not that cooperation removed all uncertainty. Residents might still fear rising costs, and a serious shortage required difficult choices. The committee therefore published monthly reports, admitted errors, and allowed members to replace representatives. When a delivery failed, staff explained the problem instead of blaming an anonymous market. Over time, people understood both the shop's usefulness and its limits. The cooperative's distinctive achievement was connecting commerce with accountable relationships. It showed that a small enterprise could be financially careful and socially generous, provided that neither neighborly affection nor a successful sales figure was allowed to substitute for honest scrutiny.","zh":"商店传达的最重要信息，不是合作可以消除一切不确定性。居民仍可能害怕成本上涨，严重短缺也要求困难选择。因此委员会发布月报、承认错误，并允许成员更换代表。配送失败时，工作人员解释问题，而非归咎于匿名市场。人们逐渐理解商店的作用与限制。合作社独特的成就是把商业与可问责的人际关系联系起来。它说明，小企业能够财务谨慎、社会上慷慨，前提是不让邻里感情或成功销售数字取代诚实审视。"}],"previous":52,"next":54});
